1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,250
China has two imperial palaces — and most people only ever see one.
{\fs13}I'm your China Travel Expert

2
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:06,500
Beijing's Forbidden City is the famous one — the Ming built it, the Qing ruled from it.

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,750
But the Qing built their own first, up north: the Shenyang Imperial Palace.

4
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:13,000
Work on their Shenyang capital began in 1625, under founders Nurhaci and Hong Taiji.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,250
The whole site is UNESCO-listed — far smaller than Beijing's, and nowhere near the crowds.

6
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:19,500
So which would you walk — the famous one, or the one that started it all?
